Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 029/138] Input: apple_z2 - Add support for the Apple N1
 (iPhone 6)

The N1 in the iPhone 6 speaks the Z2 protocol with these differences:
- power on: analog and digital supplies, the 32 kHz clock, a wake word
  while held in reset, and an HBPP bootloader probe after reset release
- the A8 SPI controller is 8 bits per word only, so blobs are byte
  swapped, and DATA packets get the 18 e1 sync prefix
- DATA packets and memory writes are acknowledged and checked, the
  calibration request is acknowledged after the following delay
- calibration goes out in chunks of at most 0x3f0 bytes, preceded by a
  proximity calibration blob; the blob header must be exactly 10 bytes
- frames carry checksums on both the length reply and the data phase,
  and the counter only advances after a good frame
- contact records start at hdr[2] + hdr[14] with a record size at hdr[17]

The firmware file gets two new records: a proximity calibration upload
and a delay.

Tested on the iPhone 6 (N61): ~60 frames/s, multi-finger, full panel
range, correct orientation.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
